// How items sit in a survivor's hand (read by the client: crates/client/src/held.rs).
//
// Anything held is drawn in the hand's grip frame: the grip at the origin, the item pointing along
// +Z, its top +Y, +X to the right of the fist. A held model is made that way; an item with only a
// ground model, or none, is laid along +Z and centred in the fist. A grip here then moves the item
// in that frame (`offset`, metres), turns it (`turn`, degrees about X, then Y, then Z) and scales
// it (`scale`), so an item that sits wrong is put right without code. Every field is optional.
//
// A release build's models have grips of their own (release-models/held/grips.ron), read over
// these, since a grip belongs to the model it fits.
//
//   "kitchen_knife": (offset: (0.0, 0.0, -0.02), turn: (0.0, 0.0, 90.0), scale: 1.0),
//
// Food being eaten with no entry here is moved out of the face by `held::EATING`; an entry
// replaces that (these two were tuned against the eating clip).
{
    "tinned_beans": (offset: (0.08, 0.0, 0.0), scale: 1.3),
    "chocolate_bar": (offset: (0.08, 0.0, -0.04), scale: 1.3),
}
